WEBVTT

00:55.930 --> 01:01.311
CHAPTER 12

02:04.124 --> 02:05.792
Do you want some toast? I made them.

02:05.875 --> 02:07.836
- What do you want on your toast?
- No, it's okay.

02:07.919 --> 02:09.504
While my bestie burned
eight pieces of toast,

02:09.587 --> 02:11.548
I did the laundry and cleaned the house.
What a morning!

02:11.631 --> 02:13.424
On the other hand, you were fast asleep.

02:15.385 --> 02:16.427
Why didn't you wake me?

02:16.511 --> 02:18.304
I even slapped your face to wake you up,

02:18.388 --> 02:20.890
but you kept sleeping
like the princess in Sleeping Beauty.

02:20.974 --> 02:22.725
Princess.

02:22.809 --> 02:25.061
If you want to wake a princess,
you need to kiss her.

02:27.605 --> 02:28.439
I did.

02:31.776 --> 02:32.694
By the way,

02:33.444 --> 02:36.197
shouldn't we name the characters first?

02:38.783 --> 02:41.828
- He’s a guy who has no sense of self.
- Okay.

02:41.953 --> 02:44.622
She’s an emotionless princess
who is just like an empty can.

02:44.706 --> 02:45.707
Okay.

02:45.915 --> 02:49.210
- And he's--
- Those aren't names.

02:49.294 --> 02:52.338
Gang-tae and Sang-tae are names.
But what you just said aren't names.

02:52.422 --> 02:54.173
Today's my day off.

02:54.257 --> 02:56.050
They don't need names. That's the trend.

02:56.134 --> 02:58.636
"Trend"? What's that?

02:58.720 --> 02:59.679
You don't need to know.

02:59.762 --> 03:02.682
If you guys have time,
do you want to go for a ride later?

03:02.765 --> 03:05.310
- Stop asking questions.
- I'm only asking because I'm curious.

03:05.393 --> 03:06.519
Then don't be curious.

03:06.603 --> 03:08.021
Mind your language to your older brother.

03:08.104 --> 03:10.440
- I'm the boss at work.
- Don't abuse your power.

03:10.523 --> 03:13.234
- You can eat all of this yourself.
- No, I can't. It tastes horrible.

03:13.318 --> 03:15.486
- Let me know when you're done.
- Don't get on my nerves.

03:15.570 --> 03:18.156
- What did I do to get on your nerves?
- I'll be in my room.

03:18.239 --> 03:19.616
Are you asking for a fight?

03:19.699 --> 03:21.326
Gang-tae told me that fighting is bad.

03:21.910 --> 03:24.454
- He told us to hold our anger.
- I'm going, okay?

03:24.537 --> 03:27.457
We're in a meeting now,
so try to think of their names.

03:58.780 --> 04:01.407
- What are you doing?
- I'm getting ready to go to work.

04:02.909 --> 04:04.869
Today's my day off.

04:05.453 --> 04:06.496
So what?

04:08.373 --> 04:09.207
Want to hang out?

04:11.292 --> 04:13.461
Should we go for a ride on Alberto?

04:15.046 --> 04:17.882
Did your number one and two,
Sang-tae and Ms. Ko, reject you?

04:17.966 --> 04:19.884
Is that why you're asking me,
your number three?

04:21.469 --> 04:22.595
Are you upset again?

04:23.012 --> 04:24.722
Gang-tae, want to know something?

04:26.224 --> 04:27.058
What?

04:30.561 --> 04:32.230
You're sly as a fox.

04:33.398 --> 04:36.025
Whenever you need me,
you talk to me all serious

04:36.109 --> 04:39.320
and get me all worried
by looking at me with your teary eyes.

04:39.404 --> 04:42.448
But once you get what you need,
you just ignore me right away.

04:43.783 --> 04:44.909
You selfish punk.

04:47.120 --> 04:48.621
So do you not want to hang out?

04:51.332 --> 04:53.459
- Do you like me better or Sang-tae?
- You.

04:55.586 --> 04:56.754
Then is it me or Ko Mun-yeong?

04:56.838 --> 04:58.881
- You.
- Come to my restaurant.

05:04.804 --> 05:05.930
My gosh.

05:09.851 --> 05:10.935
"Sly as a fox"?

05:13.396 --> 05:14.314
Ms. Kang.

05:15.773 --> 05:16.607
Here.

05:17.817 --> 05:19.944
I heard you have weak knees

05:20.028 --> 05:21.946
because you're always cooking standing up.

05:22.030 --> 05:23.906
Ju-ri told me she's extremely worried.

05:23.990 --> 05:25.116
Here.

05:25.491 --> 05:26.826
When did I say that?

05:26.909 --> 05:29.245
Don't forget to take one every day
for your health.

05:29.329 --> 05:30.705
My goodness.

05:30.788 --> 05:33.708
It's okay.
You should give it to your parents.

05:34.500 --> 05:37.462
I already bought them a box.
It's inside the car trunk.

05:37.545 --> 05:38.921
I'm going to give it to them today.

05:40.298 --> 05:41.382
Really?

05:42.300 --> 05:47.221
My goodness, then I guess
I should take one right now

05:47.305 --> 05:49.849
to thank you for the kind gift.

05:49.932 --> 05:51.434
Yes, of course.

05:52.477 --> 05:54.729
You're way better than my daughter.

05:55.146 --> 05:56.773
Let's see. There.

05:59.150 --> 06:00.777
Are you off to see your parents?

06:01.611 --> 06:03.988
Yes, something came up at home.

06:04.447 --> 06:06.783
I should go to my room.

06:08.159 --> 06:10.203
- Thank you.
- No problem.

06:15.083 --> 06:18.252
It's nothing big.
It's just a monthly event.

06:18.669 --> 06:19.921
"A monthly event"?

06:21.255 --> 06:25.134
Yes, my dad broke three ribs
and got hospitalized.

06:25.718 --> 06:27.386
My goodness. How? Is he okay?

06:27.470 --> 06:28.471
I'm so sorry to hear that.

06:28.554 --> 06:29.514
He's lying.

06:30.014 --> 06:32.141
Mr. Lee's father is a liar.

06:32.225 --> 06:33.851
He's just like his father

06:33.976 --> 06:35.645
The apple doesn't fall far from the tree

06:38.815 --> 06:41.859
My gosh, that darn brat needs to be quiet.

06:41.943 --> 06:43.444
Did you really just lie to me?

06:46.030 --> 06:50.993
The thing is,
whenever a cousin gets married,

06:51.077 --> 06:53.079
my dad gets really jealous

06:53.162 --> 06:57.583
and makes me visit him
by making up all sorts of stuff.

06:59.752 --> 07:01.587
Going on a few blind dates

07:01.671 --> 07:03.673
is the least I can do as his son.

07:03.798 --> 07:05.299
So you're going on a blind date today?

07:05.383 --> 07:07.218
Yes, I do it once a month.

07:07.927 --> 07:09.428
That's why it's a monthly event.

07:15.226 --> 07:16.936
- Drive safely.
- Okay.

07:17.603 --> 07:20.398
Well, I'll call you.

07:28.364 --> 07:29.323
He's going to call?

07:32.493 --> 07:34.036
He's totally my type.

07:34.120 --> 07:35.746
- Should I ask for his number?
- No, don't.

07:36.372 --> 07:38.040
Look at him resting his chin on his hand.

07:38.124 --> 07:41.127
- My gosh, this is crazy. Look at him.
- He's so handsome.

07:41.210 --> 07:44.172
- Will you look at that face?
- My goodness.

07:47.717 --> 07:49.510
My dear Ms. Ko.

07:50.470 --> 07:52.805
Just like how ants are drawn to sweets,

07:53.055 --> 07:56.434
lots of women are getting ready
to hit on my lonesome friend, Gang-tae.

07:57.143 --> 07:59.979
So I ask of you to quickly visit
my pizzeria.

08:00.062 --> 08:01.814
Damn, get out of the way.

08:01.898 --> 08:04.650
I'm going to kill those darn ants. Move!

08:08.988 --> 08:11.741
Here. You can try all our toppings
with this pizza.

08:12.450 --> 08:15.828
Try the one with sweet pumpkin first.
It's sweet just like you.

08:24.337 --> 08:25.338
It's good.

08:29.550 --> 08:30.843
Want to know something?

08:31.135 --> 08:32.637
When someone's in love,

08:33.262 --> 08:36.432
the brain releases vitamins

08:36.766 --> 08:38.684
and makes that person
seem more attractive.

08:38.768 --> 08:40.269
It's "dopamine," not vitamin.

08:40.561 --> 08:43.356
Are you showing off
that you work at a hospital?

08:43.648 --> 08:46.526
Neither of us got a good education.
We're like two peas in a pot.

08:46.609 --> 08:47.902
It's "pod," not pot.

08:54.325 --> 08:56.744
- You should be careful.
- Of what?

08:56.827 --> 08:58.496
- Of women.
- What?

08:58.579 --> 08:59.580
Women who are eyeing you.

09:00.623 --> 09:02.250
But you should be more careful

09:02.750 --> 09:06.379
of the crazy woman who is after the women
who have their eyes on you.

09:06.462 --> 09:07.672
What are you talking about?

09:10.424 --> 09:11.509
Welcome.

09:13.302 --> 09:17.265
We have tons of pizza boxes
ready for you today.

09:17.348 --> 09:18.933
I'm already full.

09:21.978 --> 09:23.271
How did you know I was here?

09:36.867 --> 09:38.661
Weren't you in a meeting with Sang-tae?

09:38.744 --> 09:40.079
How is that important

09:40.162 --> 09:41.956
when you're here surrounded by ants
that are after you?

09:46.210 --> 09:47.753
I shouldn't have prepared so many boxes.

09:48.921 --> 09:51.757
Hurry up and finish your pizza
so we can get out of this ant nest.

09:52.341 --> 09:54.135
I just started eating. Give me a minute.

09:55.344 --> 09:56.178
Goodness.

09:56.262 --> 09:58.055
OK VEGETABLE GARDEN

09:58.139 --> 09:59.890
Hello. Hi.

10:00.391 --> 10:01.475
Hello.

10:03.060 --> 10:06.939
Hello, tree.
It's a beautiful morning, isn't it?

10:07.356 --> 10:09.775
Oh, hello.

10:10.401 --> 10:15.197
You guys might not look the same,
but you're all birds.

10:15.281 --> 10:17.074
So don't fight, okay?

10:18.200 --> 10:21.704
You guys are so adorable and kind.
I'll be off now.

10:21.787 --> 10:23.664
Bye, tree.

10:24.999 --> 10:26.083
He's here.

10:27.293 --> 10:29.545
I thought he might not return
because he was upset with me.

10:35.426 --> 10:36.594
Ms. Park.

10:37.511 --> 10:38.679
You wanted to see me?

10:39.347 --> 10:41.432
I wanted to ask you something.

10:41.891 --> 10:42.892
Sure.

10:42.975 --> 10:45.728
Why did you get rid of
Ms. Park Ok-ran's bed already?

10:46.604 --> 10:48.814
- Because she can't come back.
- What do you mean?

10:50.775 --> 10:53.277
Patients who run away
rarely come back of their own will.

10:53.361 --> 10:54.904
And we have a long waiting list.

10:56.322 --> 10:59.408
Let's not do the same
with Mr. Ko Dae-hwan's bed.

10:59.950 --> 11:01.911
Don't call hospice either.

11:02.912 --> 11:05.456
We should let him stay here.

11:06.332 --> 11:08.668
Yes, I already told our staff to do that.

11:08.751 --> 11:10.252
Gosh, that was fast.

11:13.589 --> 11:14.757
But sir.

11:16.550 --> 11:17.676
Why do you think

11:19.053 --> 11:22.556
Mr. Ko Dae-hwan acted out
when he saw Ms. Park Ok-ran that day?

11:23.140 --> 11:25.851
It's most likely that he had delusions.

11:27.019 --> 11:29.522
I'm guessing he mistook her for his wife.

11:29.605 --> 11:31.148
The writer, Do Hui-jae?

11:31.232 --> 11:33.609
It seems like he hated his wife

11:35.403 --> 11:37.405
- and feared her at the same time.
- Why?

11:39.031 --> 11:42.201
Apparently, she killed someone.

11:44.203 --> 11:45.663
Who did she kill?

11:47.665 --> 11:48.791
Hello.

11:49.208 --> 11:52.002
- Hey, Sang-tae.
- Good morning, Ms. Park.

11:52.086 --> 11:54.004
- Hi. Sit here.
- Okay.

11:55.047 --> 11:56.674
I'll leave you guys to talk.

11:57.299 --> 11:58.926
- It's nice to see you.
- Yes.

12:00.386 --> 12:02.680
- No!
- I want some, too.

12:05.057 --> 12:07.685
I hate kids and animals.

12:08.436 --> 12:10.938
- Why?
- They're unreasonable,

12:11.021 --> 12:12.356
they whine all the time,

12:12.440 --> 12:14.108
and they always beg for love.

12:14.191 --> 12:15.317
That's why I like them.

12:16.402 --> 12:18.654
They make me care for them
because they're unreasonable.

12:19.989 --> 12:21.949
It's cute to see them whine.

12:24.285 --> 12:27.746
And because they beg for love,
it makes me grow fond of them.

12:30.708 --> 12:31.667
Just like you.

12:36.589 --> 12:37.715
I will not have your kids.

12:40.759 --> 12:42.052
Don't expect that from me.

12:42.470 --> 12:44.472
I don't want to be jealous of my child.

12:49.226 --> 12:50.394
Come here.

12:57.610 --> 12:58.444
Closer.

13:08.454 --> 13:10.289
Not everyone can be a mother, you know.

13:10.706 --> 13:11.582
Gosh.

13:13.167 --> 13:14.335
Darn, that punk.

13:16.253 --> 13:17.630
- Wait.
- I want that one.

13:18.255 --> 13:20.549
Min-jae, sit down. Come here and sit.

13:22.551 --> 13:25.179
- There you go. Is it yummy?
- Yes.

13:25.429 --> 13:27.097
You eat so well.

13:43.447 --> 13:44.782
Are you still upset

13:44.865 --> 13:47.284
that I refused to pay
for a mural with no butterflies?

13:47.368 --> 13:50.162
A... A promise isn't something
you can take so lightly.

13:50.246 --> 13:52.873
You need to keep your promise.
That's only the right thing to do.

13:56.752 --> 13:58.921
I just want you to stop

14:00.256 --> 14:03.676
running away from butterflies.

14:05.219 --> 14:06.929
Since you've always been running away,

14:07.054 --> 14:08.847
Gang-tae has had to go through
tough times.

14:09.306 --> 14:10.683
But... Butterflies...

14:13.060 --> 14:14.812
I'm scared of them.
I don't like butterflies.

14:17.231 --> 14:18.732
Let me tell you something interesting.

14:19.316 --> 14:20.317
Sure.

14:21.026 --> 14:24.321
In ancient Greek,
the word butterfly is psyche.

14:24.905 --> 14:25.906
Psyche?

14:25.990 --> 14:27.700
Do you know what they symbolized?

14:30.870 --> 14:33.122
- They were a symbol of "cure."
- "Cure."

14:33.998 --> 14:36.166
Not all butterflies are scary.

14:36.250 --> 14:40.129
There are many butterflies
that are good and can cure people.

14:40.713 --> 14:43.424
So instead of being so impatient,

14:44.133 --> 14:47.261
why don't we both try
and overcome the fear together?

14:48.804 --> 14:49.847
"Cure."

14:50.222 --> 14:53.684
If we keep trying,
there might be a butterfly

14:54.852 --> 14:58.439
flying around in your mural one day.

14:59.356 --> 15:00.691
Yes. Cure.

15:06.906 --> 15:07.948
Cure.

15:14.079 --> 15:17.291
Is your next book going to be based
on my brother's drawing?

15:17.541 --> 15:19.460
Is it about kids going on a trip
in a camping car?

15:19.543 --> 15:21.587
It's about us. The three of us.

15:22.463 --> 15:24.381
Am I the guy with no sense of self?

15:24.590 --> 15:26.592
And are you the emotionless princess?

15:26.675 --> 15:27.718
Yes.

15:28.510 --> 15:29.595
Then what about my brother?

15:29.678 --> 15:31.680
He's a guy who's trapped inside a box.

15:35.601 --> 15:36.977
What do they do on that trip?

15:39.730 --> 15:44.193
They meet people who are weirder
and a lot more deficient than they are.

15:45.527 --> 15:47.821
- What happens after that?
- That'd be a spoiler. No more.

15:51.575 --> 15:53.243
- It sounds fun.
- Of course.

15:53.994 --> 15:55.579
I'm the writer.

15:58.916 --> 16:02.419
I hope it's going to be
a happy ending this time.

16:03.754 --> 16:04.588
Me too.

16:13.847 --> 16:15.265
By the way, where are we going?

16:16.100 --> 16:17.893
To buy bread.
You burned it all this morning.

16:19.144 --> 16:20.145
I see.

16:24.274 --> 16:27.236
Look at all this stuff.
I've never been to a place like this.

16:28.362 --> 16:29.405
I want this.

16:30.614 --> 16:31.448
Just get one.

16:32.032 --> 16:33.492
I thought about it, and I think

16:33.575 --> 16:35.452
it'd be nice to have a son
who looks like you.

16:37.955 --> 16:39.623
I don't think I'll get jealous.

16:39.873 --> 16:41.417
Let's have a son.

16:43.043 --> 16:45.629
You really need to stop
getting ahead of yourself.

16:47.840 --> 16:50.342
Why? What's wrong? Let's have a son.

16:50.426 --> 16:52.302
Let's have a son! I want a son!

16:53.178 --> 16:54.722
Why won't you cooperate?

16:54.805 --> 16:56.306
I want your cooperation!

16:56.390 --> 16:58.892
- Gosh, be quiet.
- He must not want a baby.

16:58.976 --> 17:00.394
I wonder why he doesn't want one.

17:00.477 --> 17:02.980
I wonder why he won't cooperate.
He looks completely healthy.

17:03.105 --> 17:05.399
Stop talking about having a baby.
Just go and get some milk.

17:21.123 --> 17:23.083
- Ju-ri.
- Yes?

17:23.792 --> 17:26.754
Did you hear?
Dr. Kwon is getting married soon.

17:26.837 --> 17:27.921
He wasn't seeing anyone.

17:28.005 --> 17:30.299
He's marrying the woman he met
on a blind date last month.

17:30.883 --> 17:32.426
- That quickly?
- Come on.

17:32.509 --> 17:34.386
When you're at his age,
you just get married

17:34.470 --> 17:35.471
if everything seems okay.

17:37.598 --> 17:40.350
Were you guys talking about me?

17:41.018 --> 17:42.936
Then let me just cut to the chase.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.146
Surprise.

17:49.318 --> 17:51.320
Everything's proceeding so quickly.

17:52.946 --> 17:56.867
My ideal type showed up on the blind date.

18:05.084 --> 18:07.211
Should I leave Sang-tae's art supplies
in the study?

18:13.592 --> 18:14.426
Let me go.

18:15.010 --> 18:17.429
When are we going to start
using the same room?

18:18.514 --> 18:20.390
Why would I do that?
I sleep with Sang-tae.

18:21.141 --> 18:22.142
Let go of me.

18:22.976 --> 18:24.144
I'm home.

18:26.146 --> 18:27.731
Let go of me right now.

18:27.815 --> 18:30.234
Sang-tae! We're over here!

18:32.611 --> 18:34.029
Okay, fine. Let's hang out later.

18:34.113 --> 18:35.447
In my room?

18:36.365 --> 18:37.616
Yes, in your room.

18:41.453 --> 18:42.496
I'll be waiting for you.

19:09.690 --> 19:10.941
I'll call you.

19:28.000 --> 19:29.126
Yes, Mr. Lee.

19:30.502 --> 19:32.629
We have the overall storyline.

19:32.713 --> 19:35.716
I'll ask Mr. Moon about the illustrations.

19:38.468 --> 19:41.388
I came up with a list of places
we can go for research.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.932
It's near the art library.

19:45.267 --> 19:47.603
Okay. Bye, Mr. Lee.

19:54.193 --> 19:55.319
Was that Mr. Lee?

19:56.403 --> 19:57.237
Yes.

19:58.280 --> 20:00.032
Did he say anything in particular?

20:00.908 --> 20:02.117
Like what?

20:03.827 --> 20:04.953
No, never mind.

20:08.373 --> 20:11.919
Mr. Lee's blind date
apparently looked like Song Hye-kyo.

20:12.419 --> 20:14.796
His ideal type of woman
is someone who looks like her.

20:15.797 --> 20:19.051
That guy falls in love so easily.
He really got lucky this time.

20:22.804 --> 20:25.891
Butterfly is psyche,
and it symbolizes "cure."

20:25.974 --> 20:27.684
Butterflies that cure are good.

20:29.561 --> 20:31.313
- Did the director tell you that?
- Yes.

20:32.064 --> 20:34.024
"Stop running away
and face the butterflies

20:34.107 --> 20:37.319
so that Gang-tae won't have to go through
tough times anymore."

20:37.861 --> 20:39.446
Do you really think you can do that?

20:44.201 --> 20:46.703
Is... Is this expensive?

20:46.787 --> 20:48.956
How... How much is all this?

20:51.792 --> 20:53.627
Sell lots of books and pay me back.

20:54.878 --> 20:56.046
I'm going to take a shower.

20:57.047 --> 21:00.342
Psyche symbolizes "cure."

21:01.134 --> 21:04.054
There are tons of good butterflies.
There are tons of them.

21:04.137 --> 21:07.349
There are tons of good butterflies.
Psyche symbolizes "cure."

21:17.276 --> 21:18.318
No.

21:20.737 --> 21:22.531
I don't need a pillow.
I can lay on his arm.

21:39.298 --> 21:42.009
You came running
without even drying your hair.

21:55.147 --> 21:56.273
Come here and sit down.

21:59.526 --> 22:01.695
You really don't listen.

22:01.778 --> 22:03.822
This is a lot of alcohol.

22:32.476 --> 22:34.686
My brother started getting counseling--

22:34.770 --> 22:37.022
I forbid you to talk about your brother.

22:37.105 --> 22:38.398
If you do, drink an entire glass.

22:40.275 --> 22:41.735
Then you can't cuss.

22:42.402 --> 22:43.904
If you do, drink an entire glass.

22:43.987 --> 22:44.821
Deal.

22:45.447 --> 22:48.325
Shit, my damn head hurts like hell.

22:48.408 --> 22:50.452
Why am I so freaking dizzy? Damn it.

22:54.331 --> 22:55.665
Look at you swear.

22:58.960 --> 22:59.920
You should go to bed.

23:09.429 --> 23:10.639
I'm...

23:13.892 --> 23:14.726
so happy.

23:17.354 --> 23:21.775
I'm so happy that you and Sang-tae

23:22.984 --> 23:26.488
live here with me now.

24:00.897 --> 24:01.940
Good night.

25:13.970 --> 25:15.472
I WILL COME FOR YOU SOON

25:19.351 --> 25:22.062
No, I'm talking about Ms. Park Ok-ran.

25:22.145 --> 25:24.314
Why did she go there?

25:25.398 --> 25:27.192
There's no way she escaped

25:27.275 --> 25:30.153
just to wish Ms. Ko a happy birthday.

25:40.413 --> 25:43.250
The butterfly said it'd kill me as well.

25:43.333 --> 25:45.627
It'll kill me!

25:45.710 --> 25:47.420
Those butterflies!

25:47.504 --> 25:49.005
They said they'll kill me.

25:49.089 --> 25:51.383
The butterflies will kill me!

25:51.466 --> 25:53.843
They're coming to kill me!

26:00.183 --> 26:04.396
I WILL COME FOR YOU SOON

27:54.964 --> 27:57.759
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

28:00.553 --> 28:04.641
My gosh, I hope you spend
a longer time outside this time.

28:04.849 --> 28:07.018
Don't come back in just a few hours.

28:07.852 --> 28:10.397
Don't worry. I'll see you later.

28:11.564 --> 28:13.775
- You should eat a lot of delicious stuff.
- Okay.

28:18.905 --> 28:20.407
I bet he's just going to get on a bus

28:20.490 --> 28:22.200
and come back after circling around a bit.

28:23.034 --> 28:24.035
Yes, probably.

28:24.661 --> 28:27.831
But how did he end up
doing something like that

28:28.248 --> 28:29.624
when he can't even kill an ant?

28:31.334 --> 28:33.837
- What do you mean?
- Mr. Kan told me everything.

28:34.087 --> 28:36.339
He told me he killed so many people.

28:36.923 --> 28:38.174
Is that why he went crazy?

28:39.592 --> 28:41.719
He's such a weak and kind person.

28:42.762 --> 28:45.765
It wasn't something he could handle.

29:17.046 --> 29:19.382
Turn off the gas stove

29:19.466 --> 29:21.134
to save money.

29:21.217 --> 29:23.178
We need to save gas to save money.

29:25.305 --> 29:26.598
I forgot.

29:27.056 --> 29:29.851
Your... Your eyes are red.

29:29.934 --> 29:32.520
Did... Did you not sleep well?
You have the eyes of a rabbit.

29:33.646 --> 29:35.565
No, I slept well.

29:39.611 --> 29:41.863
You have counseling today, right?

29:41.946 --> 29:45.617
Yes... Yes, I have counseling.
I... I have counseling today.

29:45.700 --> 29:49.537
Butterfly is psyche,
and it symbolizes "cure."

29:51.372 --> 29:52.624
It symbolizes "cure"...

29:56.920 --> 29:58.213
But I'm still scared of them.

30:01.341 --> 30:03.927
What... What if the butterfly
appears again?

30:04.010 --> 30:05.845
We'll... We'll have to move again.

30:12.435 --> 30:13.478
Sang-tae.

30:15.355 --> 30:16.523
Let's stop

30:18.399 --> 30:19.651
running away.

30:20.735 --> 30:21.694
But the butterflies...

30:23.071 --> 30:25.615
You know that I'm good at fighting, right?

30:25.698 --> 30:27.575
Yes, you're a great fighter.

30:27.659 --> 30:29.536
You have a red belt in taekwondo.

30:29.619 --> 30:31.746
You beat up all the kids who bullied me
with your kicks.

30:31.830 --> 30:33.498
You're also good at using your nails.

30:35.875 --> 30:39.838
So from now on, if you're scared,
just hide behind me.

30:41.339 --> 30:44.300
But... But I'm your big brother.
I'm an adult.

30:44.384 --> 30:45.760
If I hide behind my little brother,

30:45.844 --> 30:47.637
that would make me... What's it called?

30:47.720 --> 30:48.721
A scaredy-cat?

30:51.015 --> 30:52.141
It's okay.

30:52.684 --> 30:56.062
I've been hiding behind you all my life.

30:57.188 --> 30:58.314
Behind me?

31:17.750 --> 31:18.835
Hey, babe.

31:19.544 --> 31:21.754
Grilled meat? Sounds great.

31:22.463 --> 31:23.464
Tonight?

31:23.965 --> 31:27.302
Why did he have to say he'll call?
I can't stop looking at my phone.

31:27.427 --> 31:29.220
- Ms. Nam.
- Yes?

31:29.596 --> 31:32.432
Mr. Ko is slowly starting to recover
his cognitive orientation.

31:32.515 --> 31:35.018
- So take him for a short walk.
- Okay, ma'am.

31:35.602 --> 31:37.937
Oh, right.
Is Mr. Moon working the day shift today?

31:38.021 --> 31:39.606
Yes, he got here a few minutes ago.

31:52.410 --> 31:53.870
I WILL COME FOR YOU SOON

31:55.955 --> 31:57.165
Mr. Moon.

31:59.959 --> 32:01.502
What? What is that?

32:02.795 --> 32:04.797
Did you receive
a love letter or something?

32:04.881 --> 32:06.382
- Come on. Show me.
- It's nothing.

32:07.967 --> 32:08.801
What's the matter?

32:10.053 --> 32:12.889
Oh, you see...

32:13.348 --> 32:16.476
I went into room 201 while doing
my rounds earlier in the morning

32:18.853 --> 32:20.355
and found a dangerous item in the room.

32:21.898 --> 32:24.192
Gosh. I have to say,
Mr. O Cha-yong always does

32:24.275 --> 32:27.445
such a clumsy job when he's checking
the patients' belongings, doesn't he?

32:28.821 --> 32:29.906
I'm sorry.

32:30.490 --> 32:31.824
I'll train him better.

32:33.409 --> 32:36.204
Can you do another thorough check
on the rooms on the second floor, then?

32:36.788 --> 32:38.373
- Sure, no problem.
- Here.

32:41.668 --> 32:42.877
You must be getting tired.

32:43.294 --> 32:45.046
Would you like to sit down for a moment?

32:58.518 --> 32:59.602
Will I

33:02.063 --> 33:04.107
die soon?

33:07.235 --> 33:08.778
Have I been

33:10.446 --> 33:11.906
punished enough?

33:22.291 --> 33:24.168
"Years went by,
and the boy became an adult.

33:24.252 --> 33:25.503
He no longer had nightmares.

33:25.586 --> 33:28.923
But for some strange reason,
he wasn't happy at all.

33:29.132 --> 33:30.383
One night--"

33:30.466 --> 33:31.509
Headed to the hospital?

33:31.592 --> 33:33.261
Yes. Hello!

33:33.344 --> 33:36.973
Oh, you're wearing
something different today. Nice clothes.

33:37.056 --> 33:39.851
- Yes, I am.
- You look very young today.

33:40.476 --> 33:42.895
By the way, how old are you?

33:42.979 --> 33:44.897
Me? I'm 70.

33:44.981 --> 33:49.110
You're 70? You're older than me.
You're an adult.

33:49.193 --> 33:50.528
I am an adult indeed.

33:51.237 --> 33:53.865
Being an adult isn't always great.

33:53.948 --> 33:55.783
Right, I agree.

33:56.826 --> 33:57.910
- Oh, look!
- Do you want this?

33:57.994 --> 33:59.495
Thank you.

34:01.748 --> 34:04.500
Right, the mural.

34:04.876 --> 34:05.835
It looks amazing.

34:05.918 --> 34:09.464
It's amazing. It looks super cool.

34:09.547 --> 34:13.885
But Director O Ji-wang wouldn't pay me
because I refused to draw butterflies.

34:13.968 --> 34:16.220
He is not a man of his word.

34:16.304 --> 34:19.057
Why can't you just draw some butterflies?

34:21.601 --> 34:23.227
I'm scared of butterflies.

34:23.311 --> 34:24.145
Why?

34:24.395 --> 34:27.273
Do you have a bad memory
of butterflies or something?

34:34.614 --> 34:37.075
Don't let the past trap you,

34:37.158 --> 34:38.159
or you'll end up like me.

34:39.243 --> 34:40.536
Look at me.

34:40.620 --> 34:42.497
I can't go back out into the world.

34:43.039 --> 34:44.916
I'll always be stuck in the hospital.

34:46.709 --> 34:47.752
The past can trap me?

34:48.336 --> 34:49.212
Yes.

34:50.713 --> 34:52.965
Then I can just open the door and get out.

34:54.133 --> 34:55.134
No, you can't.

34:55.885 --> 34:57.220
You won't be able to see the door.

35:00.681 --> 35:03.267
You can't get out
once you're trapped in the past.

35:04.060 --> 35:05.645
Don't end up like me.

36:25.558 --> 36:27.935
What's wrong? Are you not feeling well?

36:28.227 --> 36:29.645
Do your ears hurt?

36:29.729 --> 36:31.147
God, that sound...

36:32.398 --> 36:34.567
- Is that sound bothering you?
- That sound...

36:35.818 --> 36:37.904
This sound? This sound...

36:58.925 --> 37:01.969
Sir! What's wrong?

37:04.805 --> 37:06.057
Are you okay, sir?

37:06.933 --> 37:08.893
It's okay. You're okay.

37:08.976 --> 37:10.728
You're okay. It's all right.

37:10.811 --> 37:13.731
Could you please call
OK Psychiatric Hospital right away?

37:13.814 --> 37:15.483
You're okay. You're safe.

37:15.566 --> 37:18.694
You're okay. It's all right.

37:20.029 --> 37:21.864
You're okay. You're okay now.

37:21.948 --> 37:23.824
Count to three in your head.

37:24.408 --> 37:27.703
You're okay. You're okay now.

37:27.787 --> 37:30.748
You're okay. It's all right.

37:30.831 --> 37:34.085
You're safe, okay? Everything's okay now.

37:40.925 --> 37:42.260
Director O.

37:43.427 --> 37:44.887
Can you just kill me?

37:45.471 --> 37:47.139
Don't you worry.

37:47.640 --> 37:48.766
You'll die anyway.

37:51.394 --> 37:54.647
All of us here, including myself,
will die eventually anyway.

37:55.231 --> 37:56.524
Don't be so anxious.

38:01.487 --> 38:03.823
It's okay. Try to relax.

38:11.163 --> 38:13.958
- What's up?
- Well, this...

38:14.667 --> 38:16.168
I'd like to

38:16.752 --> 38:18.170
lend this book to him.

38:18.879 --> 38:20.589
- Really?
- I'm not giving it to him though.

38:20.673 --> 38:22.633
He can borrow it.
I paid a lot of money for it,

38:22.717 --> 38:24.093
so it's mine.

38:25.177 --> 38:26.679
Okay, he can borrow and read it.

38:26.762 --> 38:27.930
Yes, I'm lending it to him.

38:35.438 --> 38:36.647
DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

38:37.398 --> 38:38.399
Come in.

38:40.651 --> 38:43.988
I must say, he sure is your big brother.

38:45.114 --> 38:49.076
Without Sang-tae's help, Mr. Kan
would've gotten in a dangerous situation.

38:49.160 --> 38:52.288
I am your big brother.

38:53.331 --> 38:54.415
Have a seat.

38:57.793 --> 38:58.794
Good job.

39:00.254 --> 39:02.506
Remember what you told me earlier?

39:03.507 --> 39:05.551
- Can you also tell your brother?
- Sure.

39:06.177 --> 39:07.470
What is it about?

39:07.553 --> 39:11.140
Mr. Kan told me
that I shouldn't end up like him.

39:12.350 --> 39:15.603
He said you can never get out

39:15.686 --> 39:17.521
once you're trapped in the past

39:18.147 --> 39:20.149
because you can't even see the door.

39:22.193 --> 39:23.319
A trauma?

39:23.736 --> 39:24.820
Yes.

39:25.321 --> 39:27.198
He fought in the Vietnam War
when he was only 20.

39:27.948 --> 39:31.327
It left him with traumatic memories.

39:34.538 --> 39:36.999
There were a lot of kids.

39:38.834 --> 39:39.919
Kids

39:41.462 --> 39:44.423
with sparkling eyes.

39:46.300 --> 39:47.718
They were adorable.

39:51.889 --> 39:54.725
I just couldn't bring myself
to look at them,

39:55.559 --> 39:56.560
so I...

39:57.895 --> 39:59.563
closed my eyes.

40:00.564 --> 40:01.524
Then I...

40:04.693 --> 40:07.822
I killed all those innocent people.

40:08.656 --> 40:11.492
I don't even know why I'm still alive.

40:12.368 --> 40:14.495
You were just following an order.

40:15.037 --> 40:16.414
You had no choice.

40:16.497 --> 40:19.708
You're nothing more than a beast
if you blindly follow such orders.

40:20.042 --> 40:21.877
A human being with a heart
would never do that.

40:24.588 --> 40:26.632
I shouldn't even call myself human.

40:32.763 --> 40:34.849
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES

40:36.392 --> 40:37.518
"So don't forget any of it.

40:38.269 --> 40:39.979
Remember it all and overcome it.

40:40.646 --> 40:42.440
If you don't overcome it,

40:43.607 --> 40:46.944
you'll always be a kid
whose soul never grows."

40:47.736 --> 40:51.574
I'm not a kid. I'm an adult.

40:56.454 --> 40:57.455
Sang-tae.

40:57.705 --> 41:00.791
Yes, I won't run away anymore.

41:00.875 --> 41:02.626
I will not run away.

41:02.710 --> 41:04.420
- My gosh.
- That's right.

41:04.795 --> 41:07.339
You're incredibly brave, Sang-tae.

41:07.423 --> 41:08.299
That's right.

41:09.383 --> 41:11.635
Then would you be able to tell us

41:12.094 --> 41:15.681
what you remember about that day?

41:20.227 --> 41:21.312
Yes.

41:24.273 --> 41:25.357
Well...

41:30.613 --> 41:31.655
That day...

41:31.739 --> 41:32.781
- I--
- Kitty!

41:34.200 --> 41:35.367
That night...

41:38.454 --> 41:39.455
Well...

41:40.080 --> 41:41.665
SEONGJIN WELFARE CENTER

41:41.749 --> 41:44.585
I have to work late from now on,

41:44.919 --> 41:46.879
so you'll have to go home with Gang-tae.

41:48.130 --> 41:49.131
Okay?

41:49.882 --> 41:51.175
Look, it's a cat.

41:51.467 --> 41:52.468
Kitty!

41:53.594 --> 41:57.014
Sang-tae, get back here.
You shouldn't go in there.

41:58.098 --> 41:59.892
Get back here, Sang-tae!

42:01.644 --> 42:03.020
Fine. I'm leaving.

42:03.812 --> 42:05.105
I'm leaving without you.

42:08.400 --> 42:09.652
Bye.

42:11.320 --> 42:12.821
Bye, Sang-tae!

42:25.042 --> 42:26.001
Kitty.

42:26.502 --> 42:27.753
Kitty?

42:54.780 --> 42:57.283
I didn't get to say this earlier.

43:00.160 --> 43:01.620
It is me

43:03.831 --> 43:05.332
who will take care of my child.

44:01.597 --> 44:04.266
My gosh, why do you look so scared?

44:05.643 --> 44:07.394
It's okay.

44:08.771 --> 44:09.772
It's all right.

44:16.528 --> 44:20.157
Yes, good boy.

44:22.117 --> 44:25.579
Do not tell anyone

44:26.580 --> 44:29.208
about what you saw or heard here.

44:31.543 --> 44:34.213
If you do, I'll kill you.

44:36.924 --> 44:39.093
Even if you run away,

44:39.968 --> 44:43.972
I will chase you down no matter what
and make sure

44:45.599 --> 44:47.768
I kill you.

44:49.103 --> 44:51.188
The... The butterfly killed Mom.

44:51.689 --> 44:53.023
Okay?

44:57.444 --> 44:58.695
Answer me.

45:00.656 --> 45:02.116
I said, answer me!

45:07.287 --> 45:11.834
There was... There was a butterfly
on that woman's jacket.

45:12.418 --> 45:14.920
There was a butterfly
sitting on her jacket.

45:16.088 --> 45:16.922
"Her jacket"?

45:19.800 --> 45:20.801
That butterfly...

45:21.760 --> 45:23.887
Do you remember what it looked like?

45:24.471 --> 45:25.639
Yes.

45:27.891 --> 45:30.102
Yes, I do remember.

45:34.440 --> 45:35.649
Well...

45:38.026 --> 45:39.027
Gosh.

45:49.913 --> 45:50.914
Actually,

45:52.291 --> 45:54.293
there was a mom butterfly.

45:55.461 --> 45:59.423
And I saw a tiny baby butterfly

46:00.007 --> 46:01.717
sitting on the mom butterfly's back.

46:02.759 --> 46:03.969
It was sitting on its back?

46:12.186 --> 46:14.021
Yes, there were two...
I saw two butterflies.

46:14.104 --> 46:18.817
The mom and the baby. Two butterflies.

46:33.415 --> 46:35.501
I think that's why we're meant to be.

46:36.210 --> 46:38.253
If someone shows up when you need them,

46:39.129 --> 46:40.672
you call that destiny.

46:42.591 --> 46:43.509
And I

46:44.426 --> 46:45.552
need you.

46:54.269 --> 46:55.395
I hope it's going to be

46:56.313 --> 46:57.940
a happy ending this time.

48:00.669 --> 48:02.170
Your book is quite engaging.

48:02.462 --> 48:03.297
Yes, I know.

48:11.972 --> 48:14.600
You heard about your father, right?

48:17.311 --> 48:18.645
How much time does he have left?

48:21.898 --> 48:22.899
Let me rephrase that.

48:25.819 --> 48:27.237
When will he die?

48:28.864 --> 48:32.659
I wouldn't be surprised
even if he passed away tomorrow.

48:35.579 --> 48:38.206
I'm sick of doctors telling me
the same thing over and over.

48:42.294 --> 48:43.587
You know,

48:44.796 --> 48:46.548
if you're okay with it,

48:47.883 --> 48:52.471
why don't we take your father out
for a walk when you have some time?

48:53.096 --> 48:54.848
- Ju-ri.
- Yes?

48:58.894 --> 49:00.145
I...

49:02.856 --> 49:04.358
don't want to.

49:16.703 --> 49:17.537
Yes.

49:17.621 --> 49:19.831
So I took off my shirt right away
and put it over his head

49:19.915 --> 49:21.708
like Gang-tae does for me all the time.

49:21.792 --> 49:25.587
Then he stopped screaming and calmed down.

49:25.671 --> 49:26.797
My gosh.

49:27.506 --> 49:29.758
Great job, Sang-tae.

49:30.092 --> 49:31.301
I'm so proud of you.

49:31.385 --> 49:32.260
I know.

49:32.344 --> 49:34.805
Yes, the cafeteria. I'm at the cafeteria.

49:34.888 --> 49:36.348
So I...

49:37.265 --> 49:39.393
Where was I?

49:40.185 --> 49:43.021
Anyway, I asked someone to call
OK Psychiatric Hospital

49:43.105 --> 49:44.648
and came here with him in the ambulance.

49:44.731 --> 49:48.860
There's a storybook that I like.
It's called The Boy Who Fed on Nightmares.

49:48.944 --> 49:50.862
- I lent him that book.
- My, how sweet.

49:50.946 --> 49:52.364
He can't keep the book though.

49:52.447 --> 49:54.741
I paid a lot of money for it,
so I can't let him keep it.

49:54.825 --> 49:58.328
Anyhow, he kept thanking me.

49:58.578 --> 50:00.539
He said he's grateful to me.
He's grateful.

50:00.622 --> 50:01.790
- Absolutely.
- Yes.

50:01.873 --> 50:02.749
Sang-tae.

50:03.333 --> 50:06.211
Let's wait for Gang-tae
and go home together.

50:06.294 --> 50:11.007
Ko Mun-yeong, she's a lot older than you.
You need to say hello to her first.

50:14.511 --> 50:15.345
Hello.

50:15.929 --> 50:17.514
Yes, hi.

50:19.182 --> 50:20.851
Shall we eat out? It's been a while.

50:20.934 --> 50:23.478
No, I want to eat at home.

50:23.562 --> 50:25.105
We shouldn't be eating out.

50:25.188 --> 50:28.316
We have to save money to live better.

50:30.110 --> 50:32.237
It looks as though

50:32.446 --> 50:34.448
the three of you are actually a family.

50:34.740 --> 50:36.616
I'm getting jealous here.

50:36.700 --> 50:39.703
No. Strictly speaking, we're not a family.

50:39.786 --> 50:42.998
Gang-tae and I have the same surname,
Moon, whereas she...

50:43.081 --> 50:44.833
What was your surname? Right, Ko.

50:44.916 --> 50:46.126
Ko and Moon.

50:46.209 --> 50:48.378
Different surnames.
And she's not on our family register.

50:48.462 --> 50:53.425
We're not a real family,
but we're like a family.

50:53.508 --> 50:56.344
- The family register isn't everything.
- What?

50:56.428 --> 50:57.554
A family is...

51:05.103 --> 51:06.813
- A family is...
- Yes?

51:08.565 --> 51:10.442
You become one
if you take a portrait together.

51:11.318 --> 51:13.111
What? A family portrait?

51:13.195 --> 51:15.781
That's right. Forget the family register.

51:15.864 --> 51:18.033
A family portrait is the proof
that you're a family.

51:21.536 --> 51:24.998
The two of you are so much alike.

51:30.712 --> 51:32.839
Our eyes... Do our eyes look alike?

51:33.465 --> 51:36.051
No, we don't look alike at all.

51:37.677 --> 51:39.888
I can't pinpoint it,
but I think there's some resemblance.

51:39.971 --> 51:41.640
You're wrong. I'm very pretty.

51:42.891 --> 51:44.518
Don't lie, Ko Mun-yeong.

51:46.353 --> 51:48.396
You cut... You cut your hair.

51:57.447 --> 51:58.615
What time do you get off work?

52:02.702 --> 52:03.829
What happened to your hand?

52:05.330 --> 52:06.665
I hurt it while working.

52:07.165 --> 52:08.959
Who's the jerk that did this to you?

52:09.042 --> 52:10.210
Who did this?

52:13.088 --> 52:14.214
I'm asking you who did it.

52:24.432 --> 52:25.433
What's going on?

52:26.768 --> 52:27.769
Are you mad at me?

52:30.105 --> 52:33.441
Am I going bonkers again
without being considerate

52:33.650 --> 52:34.985
of your feelings

52:35.110 --> 52:36.736
like an empty can?

52:43.869 --> 52:45.078
I'm just tired.

52:47.289 --> 52:48.832
I didn't get much sleep last night.

52:56.631 --> 52:58.049
Go home with Sang-tae.

52:58.842 --> 53:00.385
I have to work the night shift as well.

53:02.512 --> 53:04.639
Really?
Then you'll probably be off tomorrow.

53:04.723 --> 53:05.557
That's great.

53:05.640 --> 53:08.393
The two of us and Sang-tae
should take a family portrait tomorrow.

53:17.152 --> 53:20.071
I already made an appointment
at a fancy photo studio.

53:20.405 --> 53:23.074
We should stop by a tailor shop on the way
and buy a couple of suits.

53:25.410 --> 53:26.453
Maybe another time.

53:27.287 --> 53:29.372
- What?
- Let's do it some other day.

53:30.248 --> 53:32.208
- Not tomorrow.
- But I already made an appointment.

53:33.084 --> 53:35.003
- Cancel it.
- No, I don't want to.

53:35.086 --> 53:36.963
Let's not put it off
and just do it tomorrow.

53:37.047 --> 53:39.966
We have to take a family portrait together
to become a real family.

53:40.050 --> 53:41.301
Leave!

53:46.890 --> 53:47.849
Please.

53:48.934 --> 53:50.101
Just leave.

53:53.647 --> 53:54.648
Please.

53:59.277 --> 54:00.403
I have to work.

54:49.244 --> 54:52.497
I'm going to take a photo!
I have to look cool.

54:52.580 --> 54:55.625
One... One, two, three.

55:00.088 --> 55:01.589
One, two, three. Look cool.

55:01.673 --> 55:04.092
One, two, three.

55:12.100 --> 55:15.270
What do I do to look cool?
One, two, three.

55:16.730 --> 55:19.065
Jeez, why the heck is he mad at me again?

55:19.149 --> 55:20.608
I mean, just why?

55:21.776 --> 55:24.904
Darn it. Yesterday was so nice.

55:25.905 --> 55:27.907
We drank together all night.

55:29.701 --> 55:31.411
Did I do something silly when I was drunk?

55:34.914 --> 55:36.458
Why is he angry? Just why?

55:36.958 --> 55:39.711
Was that a soliloquy or a question for me?

55:39.794 --> 55:42.422
I'm asking because
I can't quite figure it out.

55:43.965 --> 55:46.092
Did you order ten boxes of pizza
at this late hour

55:46.176 --> 55:48.303
just to make me come all the way here

55:48.386 --> 55:50.263
because you wanted to know why he's angry?

55:50.388 --> 55:51.639
It's obviously not because

55:51.723 --> 55:54.350
I wanted to eat ten boxes of pizza
in the middle of the night.

55:55.643 --> 55:56.644
Why?

55:57.145 --> 55:58.605
Why is Gang-tae upset?

55:59.064 --> 56:00.565
You must know since you're his bestie.

56:15.622 --> 56:17.749
He never really opens up to anyone.

56:19.084 --> 56:23.129
Do you know how I've managed
to stay close to him all these years?

56:26.466 --> 56:27.801
By having no idea of

56:29.844 --> 56:31.846
what goes on in his mind
or how he really feels.

56:34.099 --> 56:38.061
You see, Gang-tae is an expert
at hiding his feelings.

56:38.812 --> 56:42.273
Nothing good will come out of
prying and forcing him

56:42.690 --> 56:44.567
to share his feelings and thoughts.

56:45.318 --> 56:47.904
All you can do is just be there for him

56:49.114 --> 56:50.365
and try to comfort him quietly.

56:53.159 --> 56:54.410
That is

56:55.954 --> 56:57.288
all I do.

57:03.002 --> 57:05.630
Obviously, he's never
even had a chance to whine

57:05.713 --> 57:07.173
or complain to his parents.

57:07.966 --> 57:10.718
He got so used to just putting up
with things and keeping it all inside.

57:12.262 --> 57:14.139
Then one day,
he realized he'd become an adult.

57:17.600 --> 57:20.103
But he's still a kid inside,
so how would you understand

57:21.396 --> 57:22.730
his feelings and thoughts?

57:24.107 --> 57:26.151
Even parents can't fully understand
their own child.

57:52.927 --> 57:55.638
ROMEO AND JULIET

58:02.145 --> 58:04.939
We look like Romeo and Juliet.

58:05.231 --> 58:08.067
You're right. The ill-fated mortal enemies

58:08.443 --> 58:10.445
who should've never crossed paths.

58:10.820 --> 58:13.448
No, they were meant to be. It was fate.

58:14.282 --> 58:15.533
It was tragic fate.

58:16.034 --> 58:18.661
ROMEO AND JULIET

58:37.430 --> 58:38.806
Your hand didn't do anything wrong.

58:40.308 --> 58:42.393
Your heart is the problem
because you can't control it.

58:46.105 --> 58:47.190
Sir.

58:47.524 --> 58:48.650
Yes?

58:50.193 --> 58:52.362
I think the "butterfly"
that killed my mom was...

58:58.034 --> 58:59.661
Mun-yeong's mother.

59:01.287 --> 59:02.288
Are you sure?

59:02.372 --> 59:03.790
The possibility that it may be true

59:07.001 --> 59:08.127
scares me.

59:09.504 --> 59:11.798
I hope I'm wrong.

59:12.840 --> 59:16.886
No, I wish I had stayed in the dark.

59:23.434 --> 59:25.103
Isn't it just too cruel?

59:27.063 --> 59:29.899
I was beginning
to feel like I could finally

59:31.442 --> 59:32.902
breathe a little.

59:36.072 --> 59:37.156
I was finally

59:39.742 --> 59:41.536
starting to get the urge to live

59:45.081 --> 59:46.874
just like everyone else.

59:51.796 --> 59:54.132
Because of that damn butterfly,

59:58.011 --> 59:59.762
I've had to

01:00:02.056 --> 01:00:04.058
crawl and suffer all these years.

01:00:06.644 --> 01:00:08.104
But how could that butterfly be

01:00:12.358 --> 01:00:14.444
her mother?

01:00:27.498 --> 01:00:28.750
I always thought

01:00:31.336 --> 01:00:33.838
I'd tear the butterfly to shreds
if I ever crossed paths with it,

01:00:36.466 --> 01:00:38.259
but I can't even do that anymore.

01:00:42.138 --> 01:00:43.389
I feel so guilty when I think

01:00:44.599 --> 01:00:45.767
about my mom and my brother.

01:00:48.227 --> 01:00:49.896
What do I do?

01:00:52.315 --> 01:00:55.985
I promised my brother
that I'd fight the butterfly

01:00:56.569 --> 01:00:57.695
in his place.

01:01:00.281 --> 01:01:01.491
I...

01:01:03.951 --> 01:01:06.287
I told him that we shouldn't run away.

01:01:11.209 --> 01:01:13.336
This is so messed up.

01:01:18.675 --> 01:01:20.385
I just want to run away.

01:01:46.077 --> 01:01:48.162
I don't want Mun-yeong
to suffer like this,

01:01:51.207 --> 01:01:52.375
so I hope

01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:57.588
she never finds out about this.

01:02:01.175 --> 01:02:03.010
I don't want her to be hurt.

01:02:07.140 --> 01:02:11.102
I don't want her to ever care
about other people's feelings.

01:02:13.312 --> 01:02:15.022
I hope she can just live without emotions

01:02:17.191 --> 01:02:19.277
like an empty can.

01:03:14.582 --> 01:03:19.212
I'm so happy that you and Sang-tae

01:03:20.171 --> 01:03:23.841
live here with me now.

01:03:26.344 --> 01:03:27.929
I used to

01:03:29.055 --> 01:03:31.557
hate this place so much.

01:03:35.186 --> 01:03:36.062
Why?

01:03:37.230 --> 01:03:40.399
Because my dad lost his sanity here

01:03:42.568 --> 01:03:43.903
and my mom

01:03:45.655 --> 01:03:47.281
died in this very house.

01:03:50.952 --> 01:03:53.120
Blood kept gushing out

01:03:55.498 --> 01:03:57.375
from her head.

01:04:00.878 --> 01:04:03.339
And my dad locked her up

01:04:05.091 --> 01:04:07.426
in the basement.

01:04:11.264 --> 01:04:12.515
But the thing is,

01:04:15.434 --> 01:04:17.353
she vanished after that.

01:04:19.564 --> 01:04:20.565
My mom vanished.

01:04:24.110 --> 01:04:25.611
She vanished?

01:04:27.029 --> 01:04:28.030
Yes.

01:04:29.740 --> 01:04:31.993
I don't know if she actually died

01:04:34.453 --> 01:04:36.289
or if she just disappeared.

01:04:38.291 --> 01:04:40.418
I guess only my dad knows the truth.

01:04:44.130 --> 01:04:45.131
If...

01:04:46.841 --> 01:04:48.759
If your mom comes back,

01:04:51.095 --> 01:04:52.597
how do you think you'll feel?

01:04:55.099 --> 01:04:56.976
I'll be terrified.

01:04:58.686 --> 01:05:00.688
And I'll feel suffocated.

01:05:01.814 --> 01:05:03.399
But you know,

01:05:06.986 --> 01:05:08.404
she is

01:05:10.406 --> 01:05:11.949
still my mom.

01:06:38.577 --> 01:06:39.787
- Is he coming?
- No.

01:06:39.870 --> 01:06:42.164
He won't wake up.

01:06:42.748 --> 01:06:45.209
He won't even answer me.

01:06:45.292 --> 01:06:47.253
He's just sleeping
with the blanket over his head.

01:06:47.336 --> 01:06:50.047
He's such a sleepyhead. A sleepyhead.

01:06:56.679 --> 01:06:58.055
I guess he's tired.

01:06:58.180 --> 01:06:59.765
Sang-tae, let's take it another day.

01:06:59.849 --> 01:07:02.435
But I'm...
I'm wearing my nice clothes today.

01:07:02.518 --> 01:07:05.688
And I got up at 6:50 a.m.,
which is so early. Very early.

01:07:05.771 --> 01:07:06.981
I even styled my hair with wax.

01:07:07.064 --> 01:07:09.316
And yesterday... Last night...

01:07:09.567 --> 01:07:12.278
I practiced so many cool poses last night.

01:07:14.113 --> 01:07:15.197
What do I do?

01:07:15.990 --> 01:07:17.199
What do I do?

01:07:20.369 --> 01:07:22.496
- Let's go, Sang-tae.
- What?

01:07:23.664 --> 01:07:25.958
Let's just go and take some photos
for the book, then.

01:07:27.668 --> 01:07:29.420
Yes, photos.

01:07:29.712 --> 01:07:30.546
Let's take photos.

01:07:31.130 --> 01:07:31.964
Yes.

01:07:38.471 --> 01:07:39.638
GANG-TAE

01:07:39.722 --> 01:07:42.767
PHOTO STUDIO ADDRESS

01:08:12.505 --> 01:08:14.423
- Hello!
- Hello.

01:08:14.507 --> 01:08:15.508
Hello.

01:08:53.379 --> 01:08:54.547
Are you okay?

01:08:54.630 --> 01:08:56.215
Are you in a bad mood today?

01:08:56.298 --> 01:08:57.967
I'm always in a bad mood.

01:08:58.050 --> 01:08:59.176
Don't worry about me.

01:08:59.260 --> 01:09:02.763
Will my photo really be included
in the book?

01:09:02.847 --> 01:09:05.266
Yes, of course. You're the illustrator.

01:09:05.349 --> 01:09:07.017
Right, I am.

01:09:07.101 --> 01:09:11.397
I practiced so many cool poses last night.

01:09:11.480 --> 01:09:13.065
- You did?
- Yes.

01:09:13.315 --> 01:09:14.358
Then show me.

01:09:15.651 --> 01:09:18.112
One, two, three.

01:09:23.450 --> 01:09:25.870
One, two... One, two, three!

01:09:32.793 --> 01:09:33.711
Sang-tae.

01:09:34.295 --> 01:09:35.212
Yes?

01:09:35.296 --> 01:09:36.881
That's all fake.

01:09:46.515 --> 01:09:48.058
You don't need to try so hard.

01:09:49.226 --> 01:09:51.604
Just relax and be yourself.

01:09:52.897 --> 01:09:55.149
That's the real Moon Sang-tae.

01:09:57.526 --> 01:09:58.819
"The real...

01:10:00.863 --> 01:10:02.156
Moon Sang-tae"?

01:10:03.240 --> 01:10:04.074
Yes.

01:10:04.658 --> 01:10:06.660
"The real Moon Sang-tae"?

01:10:18.714 --> 01:10:20.758
The lady can sit on the chair.

01:10:20.841 --> 01:10:22.551
Sir, please stand next to her.

01:10:23.969 --> 01:10:26.347
Great. Sir, could you stand
a little closer to her?

01:10:26.430 --> 01:10:28.557
- Sure.
- Nice. That's perfect.

01:10:28.807 --> 01:10:31.352
Now, look at the camera
and give me a big smile.

01:10:31.435 --> 01:10:34.688
A big smile, please.
Eyes on the camera. Here we go!

01:10:35.314 --> 01:10:37.191
- One, two--
- Oh, look!

01:10:37.274 --> 01:10:38.817
Wait. Just a second, please.

01:10:40.277 --> 01:10:43.322
My brother... My little brother is here.

01:10:43.530 --> 01:10:48.202
My gosh, my brother...
That's my real brother.

01:11:28.534 --> 01:11:29.535
I'm not

01:11:32.204 --> 01:11:33.372
too late, right?

01:11:55.060 --> 01:11:57.688
Since it's for a family portrait,
please give me a big smile.

01:11:57.771 --> 01:11:58.939
Here we go.

01:11:59.440 --> 01:12:00.441
Please smile.

01:12:00.983 --> 01:12:02.234
Okay, here we go.

01:12:02.484 --> 01:12:05.362
One, two, three!

01:12:58.040 --> 01:12:58.999
Ko Mun-yeong.

01:12:59.500 --> 01:13:02.461
If I ask you
to live somewhere else with me,

01:13:03.295 --> 01:13:04.380
will you come with me?

01:13:04.463 --> 01:13:05.422
If

01:13:06.006 --> 01:13:08.133
I were born as your mom's daughter,

01:13:08.217 --> 01:13:10.386
and if you were born
as my dad's daughter...

01:13:10.469 --> 01:13:13.180
My mom would beat you up to death
for being rude.

01:13:14.973 --> 01:13:16.350
Don't trust anyone.

01:13:18.143 --> 01:13:19.395
I don't care who it is.

01:13:20.270 --> 01:13:22.147
I will not forgive
anyone who messes with my family.

01:13:23.065 --> 01:13:23.941
Am I

01:13:25.734 --> 01:13:26.693
part of that family?
